    {
      "id": 494742,
      "username": "nikkothari22",
      "name": "Nikhil Kothari",
      "created_at": "2026-02-20T17:04:23.505Z",
      "cooked": "<p>The issue is that you might have an invoice for things like utilities (electric bill etc) which have an invoice date of let’s say the 10th of a month, but the billing cycle was in the previous month. So to accurately book expenses, you need to post it in the previous month, even though the invoice was generated later.</p>\n<p>I wanted to remove this validation earlier, but found a weird hack using doc_events to get around it. Can we remove it though?</p>",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discuss.frappe.io/nikkothari22/{size}/71132_2.png",
      "trust_level": 4,
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "like_count": null,
      "like_action": null,
